Levels marking

| **Level 1 (1–3 marks)** | **Level 2 (4–6 marks)** | **Level 3 (7 marks)** |
|---|---|---|
| Statements including limited detail which explain why natural population growth rates are high | Uses named example.<br><br>More developed statements explain why natural population growth rates<br>are high.<br><br>(**Note:** Max 5 if no named or inappropriate example) | Uses named example.<br>Comprehensive and accurate statements which explain why natural population growth rates are high, including some place specific reference. |

**Content Guide:**

(High birth rates due to.....):
Lack/use of contraceptives (availability/cost/education);
Lack of/don’t use/no contraceptives 
Religious influences;
Cultural influences;
Infant mortality;
Children sent out to work (on land/in homes/on streets etc);
Lack of pensions, etc.

(Declining death rates due to.....):
Better health care;
Improvements in sanitation;
Improvements in water supply;
More food supply, etc.

Place specific reference is likely to consist of:
Named parts of the chosen country;
Population data;
Statistics

<u>Place specific examples include:</u>

- *Locational details - where situated  Niger*
- *Specific details -*

  - *Niger has a population growth rate of 3.8%*
  - *This is due to a combination of a high birth rate and a decreasing death rate*
- *Examples of paragraphs which could be included in an answer to achieve Level 3:*

  - *In Niger the average age of marriage is low at 15.7 years. This means that women have more childbearing years and are likely to have more children. This is combined with the fact that a high value is placed on large families and only 12% of women use modern contraception. All of these factors lead to an increase in the population growth rate.*
  - *Alongside a high birth rate there is a decreasing death rate this is due to a range of factors. Better food and water supply together with improved access to healthcare means that people are living longer and the death rate is decreasing.*
  - *The combination of high birth rate and decreasing death rate leads to a high rate of natural population growth.*

